# Kept in step with the sibling srt-mobile-api repository. The two had drifted:
# this file was missing `build/` and `dist/`, the sibling was missing
# `.pytest_cache/` and `.claude/`, and neither ignored `dist/` at all -- which
# matters because `scripts/verify_distribution.py` REJECTS any archive member
# whose path has a `build` or `dist` component. A stray build tree left in the
# checkout does not just clutter `git status`; it can end up inside the sdist
# and fail the release gate for a reason nobody would look for.

# Local analysis workspaces and the APKs they are unpacked from. Never
# distributed: the app binaries are not ours to redistribute, and the unpacked
# trees carry the vendor keys this repository redacts.
#
# Anchored, for the same reason `.env` below is: an unanchored `analysis/`
# matches at any depth, so it also swallowed `docs/analysis/`. The four
# documents already tracked there stayed visible, but every file added beside
# them afterwards was ignored without a word.
/analysis/
*.apk

# Credentials. `.env` is anchored so a `docs/.env` example would still be
# tracked deliberately rather than ignored by accident.
/.env
.local-live-smoke.env

# Build artifacts. `python3 -m build` writes the first two; installing in
# editable mode writes the third; `mkdocs build` writes the fourth.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
site/

# Python and pytest scratch.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Agent worktrees and local tool state — never part of the package.
.worktrees/
.superpowers/
.claude/

.DS_Store
